## 9. Limitations and Verification Findings

> [!WARNING]
> **Proxy target** — `Late_delivery_risk` is a pre-computed flag in the dataset, not raw measured delivery outcomes. The model learns to replicate this rule-based flag.

> [!CAUTION]
> **TRANSFER is a labelling artifact.** All {{ M.verification.cancel_fraud_orders | int }} CANCELED / SUSPECTED_FRAUD orders are TRANSFER payments ({{ M.verification.cancel_fraud_share_transfer | pct1 }} of TRANSFER orders vs {{ M.verification.cancel_fraud_share_other_types | pct1 }} of other types) and all carry `Late_delivery_risk = 0` (CANCELED {{ M.verification.late_rate_canceled | pct1 }}, SUSPECTED_FRAUD {{ M.verification.late_rate_suspected_fraud | pct1 }}, other statuses {{ M.verification.late_rate_other_statuses | pct1 }}). Controlling for shipping mode, the TRANSFER late rate differs from other payment types by {{ M.verification.transfer_gap_within_mode_all | pp1 }}; with cancel/fraud orders removed the difference is {{ M.verification.transfer_gap_within_mode_clean | pp1 }}. The final model's test ROC-AUC is {{ M.verification.test_roc_auc_all | f4 }} on all orders and {{ M.verification.test_roc_auc_without_cancel_fraud | f4 }} without them.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Near rule-based label** — the highest decile is dominated by First Class orders (below); precision in the top decile is {{ M.test.precision_at_top10pct | pct0 }}, an artefact of how the label was constructed rather than genuine courier insight.

{{ @top_decile }}

| Limitation | Detail |
|---|---|
| Public logistics data | DataCo is a simulated/anonymised academic dataset, not real D2C e-commerce transactions |
| Geographic mismatch | Dataset is North America / LATAM centric; not validated on Indian last-mile logistics |
| Not Indian D2C RTO | RTO in Indian e-commerce involves courier SLAs, PIN-code reachability, COD fraud — none captured here |
| Standard Class discrimination | Standard Class ROC-AUC {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].roc_auc | f4 }} (95% CI {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].roc_auc_ci_lo | f4 }} to {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].roc_auc_ci_hi | f4 }}, signal {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].flag | raw }}) on {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].share | pct1 }} of orders |
| Segment headroom | A segment-only model does not help (below) |
| Clustered scores | {{ M.score_clusters.largest_standard_cluster_share_of_standard | pct1 }} of Standard Class orders share a single calibrated score, so ranking inside Standard Class is almost arbitrary |
| No real-time features | Live courier tracking, weather, traffic data not incorporated |

